## Candidate Lemma Refinement
For S=O union 2E, it is enough to prove that every finite component of
E_safe(1/14) has an endpoint-gate ledger that cannot be covered by both
odd branch-bad interval families.  Equivalently, any attempted cover of
E_safe by odd branch-bad intervals must expose a small active odd/even
endpoint certificate; HYP-3420/HYP-3417 owner-current labels then route
the finite exceptions, while HYP-3423 blocks topology-only closure.
